status 1
action none
$ bp read VRAM 10 log A
out 50
Breakpoint #5 logging on reads of VRAM 0x10 log A.
status 0
action none
$ bp list
out 226
  #1: write RAM 0x42 = 0x07 (enabled, hit 0x)
  #2: write RAM 0x40-0x4F changed if X (enabled, hit 0x)
  #3: write RAM 0x1 (enabled, hit 0x)
  #4: read RAM 0x42 (enabled, hit 0x)
  #5: read VRAM 0x10 log A (enabled, logged 0x)
status 0
action none
end

case uninitialised reads
target fake
covers 8,15
$ bp uninit
out 24
Usage: bp uninit <space>
status 0
action none
$ bp uninit RAM
out 59
Halting on the first read of any never-written byte of RAM.
status 0
action none
$ bp list
out 64
No active breakpoints.
  (halting on uninitialized reads of RAM)
status 0
action none
$ bp uninit UNSIZED
out 57
UNSIZED reports no size, so its writes cannot be tracked.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
$ bp uninit NOPE
out 83
Error: No memory space named 'NOPE'. Available: RAM, ROM, VRAM, IO, UNSIZED, CpuBus
status 1
action none
end

